.git
.github
.claude

# Never send local dependency/build artifacts as Docker context.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/.parcel-cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Large top-level projects not used by most deploy images.
# NOTE: recoder-agency and recoder-pm are excluded then re-included below
# because they have their own Dockerfiles that build from root context.
#
# `backend` itself must NOT be excluded: backend/Dockerfile (the self-host
# control-plane image, docker-compose.selfhost.yml) builds with the repo
# ROOT as context and does `COPY backend/ ./backend/` — excluding the whole
# directory here made that COPY fail with "/backend: not found" (verified
# 2026-10-17). Only the huge vendored OSS engine subtrees are excluded below,
# since they are optional sidecars with their own separate Dockerfiles/
# compose files and are never COPY'd by backend/Dockerfile's own logic — the
# backend TS code resolves them as degrade-safe local spawn seams (see
# backend/src/domains/engines/colbert-daemon.ts, openfang-workflow.ts) that
# no-op truthfully when the path is absent.
backend/engines/py
backend/engines/rust
apps/mobile
recoder-studio
apps/ui.giselles.ai
openclaw
recoder-chat
production-engine
deployment

# Large build artifacts not needed in Docker context.
**/.vite
**/coverage

# Test and documentation files.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/e2e
**/playwright-report
docs

# Local archives/logs/media not needed in images.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.mp4
*.mov
*.csv
logs
